# MyFantasyLeague API keys — OPTIONAL.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in the values you have.
# Add the same variables in Vercel under Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables so deployed builds pick them up. NEVER commit real keys.
#
# Paste the bare key with no quotes:   MFL_API_KEY_BSB_2026=abc123
#
# Most MFL export types used here (rosters, league, players, injuries,
# salaryAdjustments) need no key at all. The exception is playerScores, which
# some leagues gate — BSB does. Without a key BSB still works; it just falls
# back to the previous season's points.
#
# MFL issues keys PER LEAGUE PER SEASON, and this client can span two seasons
# at once (current-season points, falling back to last season before kickoff).
# Resolution order, most specific first:
#
#   MFL_API_KEY_<LEAGUE>_<SEASON>   exact league + season  (preferred)
#   MFL_API_KEY_<LEAGUE>            any season for a league
#   MFL_API_KEY                     any league
#
# Prefer the season-specific form so a rollover is additive: add next year's
# key alongside this year's rather than overwriting it, and prior-season
# lookups keep working.

MFL_API_KEY_BSB_2026=
MFL_API_KEY_BSB_2025=

# Other leagues are not gated today; add only if that changes.
MFL_API_KEY_KKL_2026=
MFL_API_KEY_KDL_2026=
MFL_API_KEY_MMH_2026=
